From 164bc4b34fbb813e45d47371c1c9518e73bbd776 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:19:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-dai: label capture channels in DMA order

A capture stream of four channels was remixed by the MFC of its stream
graph: the codec DMA source labels its channels 1..n, the stream asked
for FL, FR, LS, RS. Measured on the Yoga Slim 7x V/I feedback capture:
out0 = in0 + 0.707 in2, out1 = in1 + 0.707 in2, out2 = in3, out3 = 0,
and the low 16 bits of every word (the current) turned into noise.
Label capture channels in order so the data passes through unchanged.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
index 881c35e..14e9f05 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -237,6 +237,21 @@ static int q6apm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	cfg.bit_width = prtd->bits_per_sample;
 	cfg.fmt = SND_AUDIOCODEC_PCM;
 	audioreach_set_default_channel_mapping(cfg.channel_map, runtime->channels);
+	/*
+	 * A capture stream is fed by a codec DMA source, which labels its
+	 * channels 1..n in order. Use the same labels here, so the MFC of the
+	 * stream passes the channels through. With the playback default for
+	 * four channels (FL, FR, LS, RS) the third DMA channel was taken for a
+	 * centre channel and folded into the first two at -3 dB, the fourth
+	 * landed on the third and the last one was silent: fatal for raw data
+	 * such as the speaker V/I feedback words.
+	 */
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE) {
+		int i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < runtime->channels && i < AR_PCM_MAX_NUM_CHANNEL; i++)
+			cfg.channel_map[i] = i + 1;
+	}
 	if (prtd->state) {
 		/* clear the previous setup if any  */
 		q6apm_graph_stop(prtd->graph);
-- 
